theorem curvature_certificate_apply (X Y : V) (s : T) : ... := TD.curvature_certificate X Y s

theorem curvature_skew (X Y : V) (s : T) : TD.curvature X Y s = - TD.curvature Y X s := by
  have h1 := TD.curvature_certificate X Y s
  have h2 := TD.curvature_certificate Y X s
  have hb : D.conn.lie.bracket Y X = - D.conn.lie.bracket X Y := D.conn.lie.skew X Y
  rw [hb, map_neg, LinearMap.neg_apply] at h2
  have hsum : TD.curvature X Y s + TD.curvature Y X s = 0 := by
    rw [← h1, ← h2]
    abel
  exact eq_neg_of_add_eq_zero_left hsum
```
Wait, after `rw [← h1, ← h2]`, the goal is `(∇X∇Y s - ∇Y∇X s - ∇[X,Y] s) + (∇Y∇X s - ∇X∇Y s - ∇(-[X,Y]) s) = 0`. But `h2` after the rewrite has `∇(-[X,Y]) s`? Let me redo: `h2 : ∇Y∇X s - ∇X∇Y s - ∇([Y,X]) s = curv Y X s`. After `rw [hb, map_neg, LinearMap.neg_apply] at h2`: `[Y,X]` → `-[X,Y]`, then `∇ (-[X,Y])` → `- ∇([X,Y])`, then `LinearMap.neg_apply`... hmm, `map_neg` on `TD.nabla` (as a linear map V →ₗ (T →ₗ T)): `TD.nabla (-[X,Y]) = - TD.nabla ([X,Y])`; then `LinearMap.neg_apply`? Actually after `map_neg`, the term is `(- TD.nabla [X,Y]) s`; `LinearMap.neg_apply : (-f) x = - f x`, so it becomes `- TD.nabla [X,Y] s`. So h2: `∇Y∇X s - ∇X∇Y s - (-∇[X,Y] s) = curv Y X s`. Then `← h2` rewrites `curv Y X s` to that. And `abel` should handle the double negation. Good.

