theorem second_covariant_derivative_commutation (X Y : V) (s : T) :
    TD.nabla X (TD.nabla Y s) - TD.nabla Y (TD.nabla X s) =
      TD.nabla (D.conn.lie.bracket X Y) s + TD.curvature X Y s := by
  have h := TD.curvature_certificate X Y s
  rw [sub_eq_iff_eq_add] at h
  rw [h]
  abel
```
Check: `h : (∇X∇Y s - ∇Y∇X s) - ∇[X,Y] s = curv X Y s`. `sub_eq_iff_eq_add.mp h : ∇X∇Y s - ∇Y∇X s = ∇[X,Y] s + curv X Y s`. So `rw [sub_eq_iff_eq_add] at h` gives exactly the goal; `exact h`. So:
```lean
theorem second_covariant_derivative_commutation ... := by
  have h := TD.curvature_certificate X Y s
  rwa [sub_eq_iff_eq_add] at h
```
Wait, `rw [sub_eq_iff_eq_add] at h` rewrites the hypothesis using the iff; since `h`'s LHS is `a - b - c = d` i.e. `(a-b) - c = d`, the rewrite `sub_eq_iff_eq_add` (with `a := a-b`, `b := c`, `c := d`) turns it into `a - b = c + d`. The goal is exactly `a - b = c + d`. So `exact h` after rw. `rwa [...] at h` tries to close the goal with h after rewriting. Should work.

Per-index lemma:
```lean
theorem commutator_term (i : ι) (X : V) (s : T) :
    TD.nabla (D.metric.basis i) (TD.nabla (D.metric.basis i) (TD.nabla X s))
      - TD.nabla X (TD.nabla (D.metric.basis i) (TD.nabla (D.metric.basis i) s)) =
    TD.curvature (D.metric.basis i) X (TD.nabla (D.metric.basis i) s)
      + TD.nabla (D.conn.lie.bracket (D.metric.basis i) X) (TD.nabla (D.metric.basis i) s)
      + TD.nabla (D.metric.basis i) (TD.nabla (D.conn.lie.bracket (D.metric.basis i) X) s)
      + TD.nabla (D.metric.basis i) (TD.curvature (D.metric.basis i) X s) := by
  have h1 : TD.nabla (D.metric.basis i) (TD.nabla X s)
      = TD.nabla X (TD.nabla (D.metric.basis i) s)
        + TD.nabla (D.conn.lie.bracket (D.metric.basis i) X) s
        + TD.curvature (D.metric.basis i) X s := by
    calc TD.nabla (D.metric.basis i) (TD.nabla X s)
        = (TD.nabla (D.metric.basis i) (TD.nabla X s)
            - TD.nabla X (TD.nabla (D.metric.basis i) s)
            - TD.nabla (D.conn.lie.bracket (D.metric.basis i) X) s)
          + TD.nabla X (TD.nabla (D.metric.basis i) s)
          + TD.nabla (D.conn.lie.bracket (D.metric.basis i) X) s := by abel
      _ = TD.curvature (D.metric.basis i) X s
          + TD.nabla X (TD.nabla (D.metric.basis i) s)
          + TD.nabla (D.conn.lie.bracket (D.metric.basis i) X) s := by
            rw [TD.curvature_certificate (D.metric.basis i) X s]
      _ = TD.nabla X (TD.nabla (D.metric.basis i) s)
          + TD.nabla (D.conn.lie.bracket (D.metric.basis i) X) s
          + TD.curvature (D.metric.basis i) X s := by abel
  have h2 : TD.nabla (D.metric.basis i) (TD.nabla X (TD.nabla (D.metric.basis i) s))
      = TD.nabla X (TD.nabla (D.metric.basis i) (TD.nabla (D.metric.basis i) s))
        + TD.nabla (D.conn.lie.bracket (D.metric.basis i) X) (TD.nabla (D.metric.basis i) s)
        + TD.curvature (D.metric.basis i) X (TD.nabla (D.metric.basis i) s) := by
    calc ... same pattern with s replaced by TD.nabla (D.metric.basis i) s
  rw [h1]
  simp only [map_add]
  rw [h2]
  abel
```
Wait: after `rw [h1]`, the goal is `TD.nabla (e i) (∇X∇i s + ∇[i,X]s + curv i X s) - ∇X(∇i(∇i s)) = RHS`. Then `simp only [map_add]` distributes `∇i` over the sum: `∇i(∇X∇i s) + ∇i(∇[i,X]s) + ∇i(curv i X s) - ∇X(∇i∇i s) = RHS`. Then `rw [h2]` rewrites `∇i(∇X∇i s)` to `∇X(∇i∇i s) + ∇[i,X](∇i s) + curv i X (∇i s)`. Then goal: `(∇X∇i∇i s + ∇[i,X](∇i s) + curv i X (∇i s)) + ∇i(∇[i,X]s) + ∇i(curv i X s) - ∇X∇i∇i s = curv i X (∇i s) + ∇[i,X](∇i s) + ∇i(∇[i,X]s) + ∇i(curv i X s)`. `abel` closes. 

