```lean
theorem roughLaplacian_commutator_general (X : V) (s : T) :
    TD.roughLaplacian (TD.nabla X s) - TD.nabla X (TD.roughLaplacian s) =
      ∑ i : ι, (TD.curvature (D.metric.basis i) X (TD.nabla (D.metric.basis i) s)
        + TD.nabla (D.conn.lie.bracket (D.metric.basis i) X) (TD.nabla (D.metric.basis i) s)
        + TD.nabla (D.metric.basis i) (TD.nabla (D.conn.lie.bracket (D.metric.basis i) X) s)
        + TD.nabla (D.metric.basis i) (TD.curvature (D.metric.basis i) X s)) := by
  rw [roughLaplacian_apply, roughLaplacian_apply]
  rw [map_sum]
  rw [← Finset.sum_sub_distrib]
  exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => TD.commutator_term i X s
```
Careful: `roughLaplacian_apply` is `[simp]`; `rw [roughLaplacian_apply]` on `TD.roughLaplacian (TD.nabla X s)` gives `∑ i, ∇i(∇i(∇X s))`; on `TD.nabla X (TD.roughLaplacian s)` gives `TD.nabla X (∑ i, ∇i(∇i s))`. Then `rw [map_sum]` turns the latter into `∑ i, ∇X(∇i(∇i s))`. Then `← Finset.sum_sub_distrib`. Then `Finset.sum_congr`. But `rw` may rewrite both occurrences with one call. Then `rw [map_sum]` — there might be multiple `map_sum` matches; `rw` rewrites the first match. Should be the `TD.nabla X (∑ ...)`. Then the goal has `∑ i, ∇i∇i∇X s - ∑ i, ∇X∇i∇i s = ∑ i, RHS_i`. `rw [← Finset.sum_sub_distrib]` gives `∑ i, (∇i∇i∇X s - ∇X∇i∇i s) = ∑ i, RHS_i`. Then `exact Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun i _ => TD.commutator_term i X s)`. ✓.

